[{:seon.task/name "a-date-prints-what-reads-back"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-11-05: (pr-str (java.util.Date. 1730000000123)) answers #inst \"2024-10-27T03:33:20.SSS-00:00\" on the standing root, a literal SSS, while (str d) answers ...20.123-00:00; (read-string (pr-str d)) throws Unrecognized #inst timestamp. Printing a date through seon.print is right (seon.print.select prints .toInstant), but anything through pr-str is not, so a value holding a date (seon.db/history's :at) does not read back over the wire, and a stored row read as seon.edn.edn: Invalid number 1970-01-01T00:00:00.SSS-00:00. Cause to find in Jolt: which print-method of a Date formats it, likely clojure.instant's SimpleDateFormat pattern yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss.SSS-00:00 on a shim that does not read SSS. host/chez/java/inst-time.ss's own canonical print (pad3) is right. A change to a dependency: the owner's go, and a pin. Proof: a Jolt unit case, (= d (read-string (pr-str d))) for a date with milliseconds."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
